Build buf for GOOS=wasip1: let the unix-only files cover wasip1 too.

Reason: these files define constants and helpers for every Unix-like
platform and already list `(js && wasm)`, but not wasip1, so the wasip1
build fails with undefined identifiers (DevStdinFilePath, extraInterruptSignals,
NormalizeAndValidate, netrcFilename, isOutNotAFullPath, …). Their contents
work on wasip1 unchanged. Two of the files are in vendored modules
(buf.build/go/app, github.com/bufbuild/protoplugin); build.sh applies this
patch after `go mod vendor`.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: buf and the two modules build for GOOS=wasip1 without it.

